# Follow the design docs

Before changing admin UI, read `docs/design/DESIGN.md` and `docs/COLOR_PALETTE.md`. Implement that version. `.stitch/DESIGN.md` is the same system for Stitch, not a second palette.

Tokens live in the last `:root` and `.dark` blocks of `admin/src/index.css`. Use semantic utilities. If a color must change, update those blocks and both docs together. Do not add another theme block.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — one-off hex, custom control height, tinted metric card
<div className="h-8 rounded-2xl bg-[#2463eb]" />

// ✅ GOOD — tokens and sizes from the design docs
<Button type="button">Save</Button>
<Card className="bg-card text-card-foreground" />
```

- Controls from `@/components/ui`. Icons from `lucide-react`.
- 44px controls, 12px cards, 8px buttons, 1px borders.
- One primary action. Flat cards. No gradients, glass, or rainbow KPI fills.
- Status through `StatusPill`: attempt Completed is `ok`; activity and question-bank Completed is `pr`.
- List, settings, and dashboard stacks match the recipes in `docs/design/DESIGN.md`.
